EXPERIMENT 17 – DEFECT DETECTION USING RESPONSE ASSERTION IN APACHE JMETER

AIM
To use Apache JMeter to detect defects in a web page response using the Response Assertion.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and create a Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Set Number of Threads = 3, Ramp-up Period = 3 seconds and Loop Count = 1.
4. Add two HTTP Request samplers for the path /login.
5. Add a Response Assertion to the first sampler with pattern Login Page.
6. Add a Response Assertion to the second sampler with pattern Dashboard.
7. Add Assertion Results and Summary Report listeners.
8. Run the plan and observe the results.
TEST PLAN CONFIGURATION
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Number of Threads	3
Thread Group	Ramp-up Period	3 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	1
HTTP Request 1	Name	Login Page - correct text
HTTP Request 1	Server Name	the-internet.herokuapp.com
HTTP Request 1	Protocol / Method / Path	https / GET / /login
Response Assertion 1	Field to Test	Text Response
Response Assertion 1	Matching Rule	Contains
Response Assertion 1	Pattern	Login Page
HTTP Request 2	Name	Login Page - wrong text
HTTP Request 2	Protocol / Method / Path	https / GET / /login
Response Assertion 2	Field to Test	Text Response
Response Assertion 2	Matching Rule	Contains
Response Assertion 2	Pattern	Dashboard

INPUT
- Correct expected text: Login Page
- Incorrect expected text: Dashboard
- Number of users: 3
- Loop count: 1
OUTPUT
Assertion Results
Login Page - correct text : no failure message
(assertion passed)

Login Page - wrong text :
Test failed: text expected to contain /Dashboard/


Summary Report
Label	Samples	Error %
Login Page - correct text	3	0.00%
Login Page - wrong text	3	100.00%
TOTAL	6	50.00%

RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to detect defects in a web page response using the Response Assertion, and the results were verified.
